b45f7-a086-507a-8456-0d164d0de004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "discontinuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432901} {:answer/id #uuid "315d7d76-0771-5130-89b6-81c348c20cd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "315d7d76-0771-5130-89b6-81c348c20cd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432908} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf181985-9c1c-555e-85d4-6e60d5f94c43" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432951}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2dec04ba-d895-5497-b51c-f40bad0126da" :question/math-academy-id "q-343439" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}5, & x\\in [-6,0] \\\\ -2, & x\\in (0,6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. The Fourier series of the $12$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{3}{2}-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{14}{\\pi (2n-1)}sin\\,(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi x}{6}).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nAt $x=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\nsin\\,(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi (-3)}{6})={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-2}}\nat $x=-3,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(-3)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1}={{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite our Fourier series as\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{14}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot sin\\,(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi x}{6}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that at $x=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\nsin\\,(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi (-3)}{6})=sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-n\\pi )=(-1)^{n}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is $\\text{continuous}$ at $x=-3,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(-3)=5.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) & =\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{14}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot sin\\,(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi (-3)}{6}) \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{14}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot (-1)^{n} \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} & =-\\frac{14}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{2n-1} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{2n-1} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
